``` IX-09 | Silent Index or Sourcetype: Data Stopped Arriving
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: Detect an index/sourcetype pair that normally receives data
    every hour but has gone quiet, before a downstream alert or dashboard
    owner notices.
    Run on: SH. tstats reads only .tsidx metadata, so seven days across all
    indexes returns in seconds.
    Query: Main query
```
| tstats count where index=* earliest=-7d@h latest=now
    by index sourcetype _time span=1h
| stats count as active_hours max(_time) as last_active_hour
        sum(count) as events_7d
        by index sourcetype
| eval expected_hours=7 * 24,
       activity_pct=round(100 * active_hours / expected_hours, 1),
       hours_silent=round((now() - last_active_hour) / 3600, 1)
| where activity_pct >= 80 AND hours_silent >= 2
| sort - hours_silent
| table index sourcetype activity_pct hours_silent events_7d
